# Opinion

Meeting: 0003-improve-the-design-and-aesthetics-of-rps-arena
Agent: ArchitectA
Task: Improve the design and aesthetics of RPS Arena
Context:
- Target: refresh the RPS Arena front-end without adding frameworks; keep server-authoritative API untouched.
- Constraints: maintain 100% coverage via `npm test` (c8 --100), avoid Playwright/screenshots per instructions, and honor meeting workflow artifacts.
- Existing UI uses vanilla HTML/CSS/JS served by Node; new design must stay buildless and performant.

Position:
- Lean into reusable view utilities to keep templating deterministic and testable while improving visual polish.
- Maintain semantic structure (panels/cards) so CSS enhancements (glassmorphism, gradients) don’t harm accessibility or portability.
- Favor additive styling over structural API changes to avoid breaking existing forms/endpoints.

Recommendations:
- Introduce pure render helpers for news/leaderboard/history to decouple markup from fetch logic and enable full branch coverage.
- Refresh the layout with a sticky nav, elevated hero stats, and clearer affordances (active nav states, pill badges) using only CSS/HTML updates.
- Keep theme tokens centralized in CSS vars; avoid new dependencies and rely on Google Fonts only for typography improvement.
